  "contract": "docs/ASSET_PIPELINE.md#11-stil-tanımı",
  "note": "Twelve four-step ramps. Step 900 is the shadow side and doubles as the derived 2px outline for its family — the outline is never pure black (ASSET_PIPELINE §1.1). Step 300 is the lit side; the key light is upper-left, so 300 faces up-left and 900 faces down-right. `tolerance` is the maximum Euclidean RGB distance a pixel may sit from its nearest palette entry; `coverage` is the fraction of opaque pixels that must be within it. No two entries are closer to each other than `tolerance`, so every entry is a genuinely distinct target rather than a wasted slot. `affinityBaseline` is the mean nearest-palette distance of *uniformly random* RGB: 400 000 Monte Carlo samples against these 48 entries give 51.48, and 48 points spread through a 256-cube predict 43.7 from volume alone, so the measured figure is the honest no-information point rather than a chosen number. An asset at or above it has no demonstrable relationship to this palette. `affinityWarn` is the fraction of that baseline above which an asset is reported as off-family without failing. Replaces the 92%-within-8 conformance rule for continuous-tone art — see ADR-013.",
